   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">NLP401 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.4</span>\n<h2>Textbooks, materials & tools the university names</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Main textbooks: <strong>Coursera Natural Language Processing Specialization</strong>; <strong>Course 1: Natural Language Processing with Classification and Vector Spaces</strong>; <strong>Course 2: Natural Language Processing with Probabilistic Models</strong>; <strong>Course 3: Natural Language Processing with Sequence Models</strong>; <strong>Course 4: Natural Language Processing with Attention Models</strong>; <strong>Natural Language Processing in Action: Understanding, Analyzing, and Generating Text with Python</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 14405 (subject NLP301m, used as reference) · Decision 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 07/08/2026 · collected 09/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">NLP401 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.4</span>\n<h2>Giáo trình, tài liệu & công cụ trường quy định</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Giáo trình chính: <strong>Coursera Natural Language Processing Specialization</strong>; <strong>Course 1: Natural Language Processing with Classification and Vector Spaces</strong>; <strong>Course 2: Natural Language Processing with Probabilistic Models</strong>; <strong>Course 3: Natural Language Processing with Sequence Models</strong>; <strong>Course 4: Natural Language Processing with Attention Models</strong>; <strong>Natural Language Processing in Action: Understanding, Analyzing, and Generating Text with Python</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 14405 (môn NLP301m, dùng làm tham khảo) · QĐ 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 07/08/2026 · thu ngày 09/11/2026</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Material<br><small>Tài liệu</small></th><th>Author<br><small>Tác giả</small></th><th>Publisher<br><small>NXB</small></th><th>Year<br><small>Năm</small></th><th>Edition<br><small>Lần xuất bản</small></th><th>ISBN</th><th>Main<br><small>Chính</small></th><th>Hard copy<br><small>Bản in</small></th><th>Online</th><th>Note<br><small>Ghi chú</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Coursera Natural Language Processing Specialization</strong></td><td>DeepLearning.AI</td><td>Coursera</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>✔</td><td><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/specializations/natural-language-processing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.coursera.org/specializations/natural-language-processing</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Course 1: Natural Language Processing with Classification and Vector Spaces</strong></td><td>DeepLearning.AI</td><td>Coursera</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>✔</td><td><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/classification-vector-spaces-in-nlp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.coursera.org/learn/classification-vector-spaces-in-nlp</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Course 2: Natural Language Processing with Probabilistic Models</strong></td><td>DeepLearning.AI</td><td>Coursera</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/probabilistic-models-in-nlp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.coursera.org/learn/probabilistic-models-in-nlp</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Course 3: Natural Language Processing with Sequence Models</strong></td><td>DeepLearning.AI</td><td>Coursera</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/sequence-models-in-nlp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.coursera.org/learn/sequence-models-in-nlp</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Course 4: Natural Language Processing with Attention Models</strong></td><td>DeepLearning.AI</td><td>Coursera</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>✔</td><td><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/attention-models-in-nlp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.coursera.org/learn/attention-models-in-nlp</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Natural Language Processing in Action: Understanding, Analyzing, and Generating Text with Python</strong></td><td>Hobson Lane, Cole Howard and Hannes Max Hapke</td><td>Manning</td><td>2019</td><td></td><td></td><td>✔</td><td>—</td><td>✔</td><td><a href=\"https://library.books24x7.com/toc.aspx?bookid=147295\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://library.books24x7.com/toc.aspx?bookid=147295</a></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>Course project proposal and progress-report templates</strong></td><td>Course instructor</td><td>classroom distribution</td><td>2026</td><td>course template</td><td></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>Instructor-provided template for Report 1, Report 2, and Report 3</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Short research paper template and peer-review rubric</strong></td><td>Course instructor</td><td>classroom distribution</td><td>2026</td><td>course template</td><td></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>Instructor-provided final paper template, presentation guide, and peer-review rubric</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td><strong>Natural Language Processing with Python</strong></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td><a href=\"https://www.nltk.org/book/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.nltk.org/book/</a></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Tools</h3>\n<p>- Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab<br><br>- Python libraries: NumPy, NLTK, scikit-learn, TensorFlow / Keras, PyTorch or equivalent as needed for specialization-aligned models<br><br>- Git/GitHub for version control, experiment logs, and teamwork<br><br>- Reference manager / citation workflow (e.g., Zotero, Mendeley, or equivalent)<br><br>- Cloud/GPU server or Colab runtime as needed for project experiments</p>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">Materials with no author/ISBN (slides, exercise packs…) are usually internal files you download inside FLM with your FPT account. Buy the exact <strong>edition</strong> listed — page and exercise numbers change between editions.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Công cụ</h3>\n<p>- Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab<br><br>- Python libraries: NumPy, NLTK, scikit-learn, TensorFlow / Keras, PyTorch or equivalent as needed for specialization-aligned models<br><br>- Git/GitHub for version control, experiment logs, and teamwork<br><br>- Reference manager / citation workflow (e.g., Zotero, Mendeley, or equivalent)<br><br>- Cloud/GPU server or Colab runtime as needed for project experiments</p>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">Tài liệu không có tác giả/ISBN (slide, bộ bài tập…) thường là file nội bộ, tải trong FLM bằng tài khoản FPT. Mua đúng <strong>lần xuất bản</strong> ghi trong bảng — số trang, số bài tập đổi giữa các bản.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14405\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14405</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14405\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14405</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
